aboutte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aboutte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aboutte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duplocloud/devkit/commits/efb55d63955ec0c63ab66ad69431e80db50f5a08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:12:00Z","email":"andy@duplocloud.net","name":"Andy Boutte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:12:00Z","email":"andy@duplocloud.net","name":"Andy Boutte"},"message":"feat(run.sh): remove usage-metrics opt-in prompt and nginx toggle\n\nThe product now handles usage-metrics consent inside the UI itself, so\nthe dev kit no longer needs to ask, store a choice, or rewrite the\nserved bundle:\n\n- run.sh: drop the --metrics/--no-metrics flags, the opt-out prompt,\n  and the Metrics line in the ready banner\n- scripts/_metrics.sh, nginx/metrics-on.conf, nginx/metrics-off.conf:\n  deleted\n- nginx/default.conf: drop the metrics.conf include; it''s now a plain\n  same-origin API proxy\n- docker-compose.yml: drop the METRICS_CONF volume mount\n- .env.example: drop DUPLO_USAGE_METRICS / METRICS_CONF\n- .gitleaksignore: deleted (its only entry covered the now-removed\n  metrics-on.conf)\n- docs: PRIVACY.md, README.md, configuration.md, faq.md,\n  cli-reference.md, getting-started/install.md, quickstart.md,\n  docs/README.md, hackday/Installing DevKit.md updated to describe\n  consent as an in-product UI setting\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03f5219fccf41fee094c3cfa890a5757f6cee160","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duplocloud/devkit/git/trees/03f5219fccf41fee094c3cfa890a5757f6cee160"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duplocloud/devkit/git/commits/efb55d63955ec0c63ab66ad69431e80db50f5a08","verification":{"payload":"tree 03f5219fccf41fee094c3cfa890a5757f6cee160\nparent fef3fbde548d945b4074c05dfea6b8bdb433c278\nauthor Andy Boutte <andy@duplocloud.net> 1790554320 -0700\ncommitter Andy Boutte <andy@duplocloud.net> 1790554320 -0700\n\nfeat(run.sh): remove usage-metrics opt-in prompt and nginx toggle\n\nThe product now handles usage-metrics consent inside the UI itself, so\nthe dev kit no longer needs to ask, store a choice, or rewrite the\nserved bundle:\n\n- run.sh: drop the --metrics/--no-metrics flags, the opt-out prompt,\n  and the Metrics line in the ready banner\n- scripts/_metrics.sh, nginx/metrics-on.conf, nginx/metrics-off.conf:\n  deleted\n- nginx/default.conf: drop the metrics.conf include; it''s now a plain\n  same-origin API proxy\n- docker-compose.yml: drop the METRICS_CONF volume mount\n- .env.example: drop DUPLO_USAGE_METRICS / METRICS_CONF\n- .gitleaksignore: deleted (its only entry covered the now-removed\n  metrics-on.conf)\n- docs: PRIVACY.md, README.md, configuration.md, faq.md,\n  cli-reference.md, getting-started/install.md, quickstart.md,\n  docs/README.md, hackday/Installing DevKit.md updated to describe\n  consent as an in-product UI setting\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAAhcAAAAHc3NoLXJzYQAAAAMBAAEAAAIBAPiLwERkyNXZ7qXP5Q/Wim\nVODBOhNGOT7sm4PUb2P8dIURvqxcPmCbXFxeqGAV48cdWBkMpsF+xPYzQyUDdzASnI5XP0\nLm13grakx7UnqMgxS1FG0sI/Sq0I2eUyE9GOrXM4EozpM0Q1zCpNKzp97ac4Q9a5V0M08Q\nd2zFyw4L/4NFP/uMdtfGTHEEXqjtMD5dV27pZl+8Fi28ViYHkqMcpKPbqrH2XAEHDsEBjC\n0oKZxttXTPqWMImA+/CAMVVYu3+HW4YEaedGZm/cpZ5oGtQzdn9NKtszTAxgfFPR35Ne1B\nXxmsr0lEwjth8bIPsoA2Uv2y3OGhGOVi1jWnwYKwSZuJxsk1mOOwGj6mZtpYv9a5IZhXJc\nCkk0ftfHzK9Ur9CH/FoBsmpJsArCKEyQBiZNP8Sl9eK/PUim0INcvzb36hBtxHLhDPgeVx\nm12UxATPiHSu2kwbhp9/GtftmCOST518ohdSKKsaOOnloK07ieeD5XnTpeZT97dhwSf4oa\nCv60v8lhH3QSLoHsejSZvxI+f/vOk2I5MvVHRC+8x+Twd4R6nzkzFkcn3AubIwcUcIfi6x\ntCUwUxxwpC2BCELp/onMzNNmDS11+YHdBBb0ntQNU75pJt1eWdMmaeJ/RokcDPOCjf30rZ\ndnYS041Xz44g+CQGV61w28hRirlxdRl3AAAAA2dpdAAAAAAAAAAGc2hhNTEyAAACFAAAAA\nxyc2Etc2hhMi0yNTYAAAIAePy2dv9WtpuXCBd/sSryb3