e"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:45:54.732Z","repositoryId":1379257408,"sha":"0a91904090882d3f6ffaeb8af1adea44eaa0fc7e"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:45:54.732Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/babe3932bd7f4b46f467f51f37c07561bb2abc89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:39:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:39:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Rebuild design system on Snapchat''s palette (yellow/black/white, flat, pill)\n\nReplaces the warm terracotta/cream palette from the previous pass with a\nSnapchat-inspired one: white/near-black canvas, signature yellow\n(#FFFC00) as the single brand/accent color, 64px pill-radius buttons,\nAvenir Next (iOS system font) for type, and a flat/shadowless component\nstyle.\n\nDeliberately deviated from the reference in two places, documented in\ndocs/design-system.md:\n- Yellow is never used as a text/icon color on a light surface — #FFFC00\n  on white has too little contrast to read. It''s applied only as a filled\n  background (buttons, selected chips/tabs) with black accentText on top,\n  which is also how Snapchat''s own product actually uses it. Tab bar\n  active tint and action links moved to black/underline instead of\n  yellow-as-text.\n- Ghost Sans is Snap Inc.''s proprietary font and isn''t available to us;\n  used Avenir Next (built into iOS) instead, falling back to the system\n  font on Android/web.\n\nRadius tokens renamed to match the reference''s scale (input=5, card=8,\nbutton=64, pill=9999) and propagated through every screen''s inline\nstyles. Button press now scales to 0.97, matching the reference''s\n\"Pill press\" motion note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9","tree":{"sha":"6a84adc492988c0790c965a3491c95ef5e612e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/trees/6a84adc492988c0790c965a3491c95ef5e612e2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/commits/babe3932bd7f4b46f467f51f37c07561bb2abc89","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a84adc492988c0790c965a3491c95ef5e612e2d\nparent 8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790602782 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790602782 +0000\n\nRebuild design system on Snapchat''s palette (yellow/black/white, flat, pill)\n\nReplaces the warm terracotta/cream palette from the previous pass with a\nSnapchat-inspired one: white/near-black canvas, signature yellow\n(#FFFC00) as the single brand/accent color, 64px pill-radius buttons,\nAvenir Next (iOS system font) for type, and a flat/shadowless component\nstyle.\n\nDeliberately deviated from the reference in two places, documented in\ndocs/design-system.md:\n- Yellow is never used as a text/icon color on a light surface — #FFFC00\n  on white has too little contrast to read. It''s applied only as a filled\n  background (buttons, selected chips/tabs) with black accentText on top,\n  which is also how Snapchat''s own product actually uses it. Tab bar\n  active tint and action links moved to black/underline instead of\n  yellow-as-text.\n- Ghost Sans is Snap Inc.''s proprietary font and isn''t available to us;\n  used Avenir Next (built into iOS) instead, falling back to the system\n  font on Android/web.\n\nRadius tokens renamed to match the reference''s scale (input=5, card=8,\nbutton=64, pill=9999) and propagated through every screen''s inline\nstyles. Button press now scales to 0.97, matching the reference''s\n\"Pill press\" motion note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAzDRjLP\n0LHAudVAG9jNZUgNlDaoQg6bIEG1+Mw9TXukcdshUdW6OL0yp9E9/CYptMVDeGWzfX4LHtXQK6Vd\nlgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:39:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/babe3932bd7f4b46f467f51f37c07561bb2abc89","node_id":"C_kwDOUjXMQNoAKGJhYmUzOTMyYmQ3ZjRiNDZmNDY3ZjUxZjM3YzA3NTYxYmIyYWJjODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c","sha":"8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c"}],"sha":"babe3932bd7f4b46f467f51f37c07561bb2abc89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/babe3932bd7f4b46f467f51f37c07561bb2abc89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:51:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:51:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Set up a warm sepia/cream design system and apply it app-wide\n\nAdds docs/design-system.md documenting the palette, typography scale,\nspacing/radius tokens, and component rules, so future screen work has a\nsingle source of truth to follow instead of drifting per-screen.\n\nRewrote src/constants/theme.ts with a warm terracotta/cream palette\n(accent + accentText tokens replace the old default-blue button color)\nand a new Radius scale. Propagated it through the shared components\n(PrimaryButton, ChipSelect, ThemedText''s title/subtitle now use the\nrounded system font) and every screen that had its own inline\ntab-pill/card/input styling (home, nearby, saved, login, trip-setup,\ntestimonials, tabs layout), replacing hardcoded hex colors and radius\nnumbers with theme tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9","tree":{"sha":"4b4ff424675d79fdc249f3219ce8f8dce63bdc92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/trees/4b4ff424675d79fdc249f3219ce8f8dce63bdc92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/commits/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b4ff424675d79fdc249f3219ce8f8dce63bdc92\nparent 8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790599870 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790599870 +0000\n\nSet up a warm sepia/cream design system and apply it app-wide\n\nAdds docs/design-system.md documenting the palette, typography scale,\nspacing/radius tokens, and component rules, so future screen work has a\nsingle source of truth to follow instead of drifting per-screen.\n\nRewrote src/constants/theme.ts with a warm terracotta/cream palette\n(accent + accentText tokens replace the old default-blue button color)\nand a new Radius scale. Propagated it through the shared components\n(PrimaryButton, ChipSelect, ThemedText''s title/subtitle now use the\nrounded system font) and every screen that had its own inline\ntab-pill/card/input styling (home, nearby, saved, login, trip-setup,\ntestimonials, tabs layout), replacing hardcoded hex colors and radius\nnumbers with theme tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAbW8Fgq\nf93Evb0Hcz5+gkahTeWhXs2KsBEW31rkFIMEfZHXwleXUXbAtoh3qtdTReQYaFN8NzLwqK1jW3nT\nOg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:51:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c","node_id":"C_kwDOUjXMQNoAKDhiZTI5ZTU4M2E0YTZjOTUxMWU1NDQ1N2FhN2FkMjNhZWY5ZTk1MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55","sha":"8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55"}],"sha":"8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8be29e583a4a6c9511e54457aa7ad23aef9e950c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:36:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:36:44Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Use Deezer''s genre chart API for accurate genre-tagged tracks\n\nFree-text genre keywords (added in the previous commit) turned out to be\nunreliable: the user reported picking K-POP still surfaced jazz-sounding\ntracks. Checked a live GET https://api.deezer.com/genre response (this\nsession can''t reach api.deezer.com itself) and confirmed Deezer has no\nK-Pop/Indie/Lo-fi/Acoustic entries in its genre taxonomy at all — only\nbroad buckets. Pop=132, Rap/Hip Hop=116, Jazz=129, Classical=98 do exist\nthough.\n\nFor those four, mood-track now calls Deezer''s /chart/{id}/tracks endpoint,\nwhich returns real genre-tagged top tracks instead of hoping a keyword\nmatch happens to be genre-relevant. 인디/로파이/어쿠스틱/K-POP still use\nthe free-text fallback since Deezer has nothing more accurate to offer for\nthem, and the chart path also falls back to free-text if the chart call\nfails or comes up empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9","tree":{"sha":"8d613bd544817e92edbf4cacaf1feb5389250fac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/trees/8d613bd544817e92edbf4cacaf1feb5389250fac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/commits/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d613bd544817e92edbf4cacaf1feb5389250fac\nparent 0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790599004 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790599004 +0000\n\nUse Deezer''s genre chart API for accurate genre-tagged tracks\n\nFree-text genre keywords (added in the previous commit) turned out to be\nunreliable: the user reported picking K-POP still surfaced jazz-sounding\ntracks. Checked a live GET https://api.deezer.com/genre response (this\nsession can''t reach api.deezer.com itself) and confirmed Deezer has no\nK-Pop/Indie/Lo-fi/Acoustic entries in its genre taxonomy at all — only\nbroad buckets. Pop=132, Rap/Hip Hop=116, Jazz=129, Classical=98 do exist\nthough.\n\nFor those four, mood-track now calls Deezer''s /chart/{id}/tracks endpoint,\nwhich returns real genre-tagged top tracks instead of hoping a keyword\nmatch happens to be genre-relevant. 인디/로파이/어쿠스틱/K-POP still use\nthe free-text fallback since Deezer has nothing more accurate to offer for\nthem, and the chart path also falls back to free-text if the chart call\nfails or comes up empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOUx+F69\nD3hBo5gKXgQW24Wh2pEFOTZJO3ghIn0DUzmauDJGAveZZw9nvFQRF4+aspDS0fg9cnWcumM5TTZB\n3Ac=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:36:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55","node_id":"C_kwDOUjXMQNoAKDhmODVkNzc4M2FhOGE2ZWI2YjZlMjM2OTJmZDk1MzgyYjRmZDViNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943","sha":"0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943"}],"sha":"8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/8f85d7783aa8a6eb6b6e23692fd95382b4fd5b55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:21:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:21:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix home screen not picking up music preference edits until app restart\n\nThe trip fetch on the home screen ran in a plain useEffect keyed on\n`session`, which only fires once when the tab first mounts. Since the\ntabs navigator keeps screens mounted across tab switches, editing genres\nin Settings → 음악 취향 수정 and coming back to the home tab never\nrefetched the trip — \"다른 느낌으로\" kept using whatever\ntripMoodPreferences/tripMusicGenres were in state from the first mount\n(e.g. still 재즈 after switching to 힙합).\n\nSwitched to expo-router''s useFocusEffect so the trip refetches every time\nthe home tab regains focus, not just once on mount.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9","tree":{"sha":"4ed23b39c8580a8be6915a53f3c0f1910586b1ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/trees/4ed23b39c8580a8be6915a53f3c0f1910586b1ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/commits/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ed23b39c8580a8be6915a53f3c0f1910586b1ad\nparent fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790598072 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790598072 +0000\n\nFix home screen not picking up music preference edits until app restart\n\nThe trip fetch on the home screen ran in a plain useEffect keyed on\n`session`, which only fires once when the tab first mounts. Since the\ntabs navigator keeps screens mounted across tab switches, editing genres\nin Settings → 음악 취향 수정 and coming back to the home tab never\nrefetched the trip — \"다른 느낌으로\" kept using whatever\ntripMoodPreferences/tripMusicGenres were in state from the first mount\n(e.g. still 재즈 after switching to 힙합).\n\nSwitched to expo-router''s useFocusEffect so the trip refetches every time\nthe home tab regains focus, not just once on mount.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG0buKiW\nr1wdT/2V6ObFy0NKaEghKDliB/e4zec1K7G94y7vid/T8K3FrR2ChaBRhUPTfJaotc8/XJO2XiW0\nIgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:21:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943","node_id":"C_kwDOUjXMQNoAKDBlMGMzOTY3NDM3YmVlZDU0M2E5ZTUzOGYyODI0MDZjOTllNjk5NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092","sha":"fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092"}],"sha":"0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/0e0c3967437beed543a9e538f282406c99e69943"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/commits/fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:17:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:17:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make mood-track resilient to genre+mood combos with no search hits\n\nMore genres and moods means more combinations, and Deezer''s free-text\nsearch can legitimately return zero results for an unusual pairing (e.g.\n\"classical\" + \"epic cinematic\") even though each term alone has plenty.\nmood-track now falls back to a mood-only search when the combined query\ncomes up empty, instead of returning a 404 for that card.\n\nAlso hardened the home screen: it now uses Promise.allSettled instead of\nPromise.all when fetching the 3 cards, so one card''s fetch failing\ndoesn''t blank out the other two that succeeded — only throws (and shows\nthe error alert) if all 3 fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9","tree":{"sha":"c1bc623d25566beefa6aaffa73694ddcc380805a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/trees/c1bc623d25566beefa6aaffa73694ddcc380805a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yerinni/ai_practice/git/commits/fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092","verification":{"payload":"tree c1bc623d25566beefa6aaffa73694ddcc380805a\nparent 56ff6e176572947e91d7881287e15b76beed3a58\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790597827 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790597827 +0000\n\nMake mood-track resilient to genre+mood combos with no search hits\n\nMore genres and moods means more combinations, and Deezer''s free-text\nsearch can legitimately return zero results for an unusual pairing (e.g.\n\"classical\" + \"epic cinematic\") even though each term alone has plenty.\nmood-track now falls back to a mood-only search when the combined query\ncomes up empty, instead of returning a 404 for that card.\n\nAlso hardened the home screen: it now uses Promise.allSettled instead of\nPromise.all when fetching the 3 cards, so one card''s fetch failing\ndoesn''t blank out the other two that succeeded — only throws (and shows\nthe error alert) if all 3 fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HC1smVb7bxSwWomzaeSXo9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL/PpYy/\n2EbIY9OKKSM6cdhlPNfRfz4M+a+jJTugMOoVx/lllwak4odbQM2CQmAqmjO6Rtlqb5YSgxtkrf31\ncA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T12:17:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yerinni/ai_practice/commit/fdd70e81e128056c0e1d1506aeba2dace42df092","node_id":"C_kwDOUjXMQNoAKGZkZDcwZTgxZTEyODA1NmMwZTFkMTUwNmFlYmEyZGFj