hub.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/d313fce698982be54e22f7307a61cbe02849cbda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:10:28Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:10:28Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"a clone can be run: getting started, npm run db / dev / web, and what to do when it breaks\n\nthe readme opens with what you need, the two ways to run it (all in docker, or each piece\nfrom source), what to try once it is up, and how to run the tests. three scripts replace\nthe steps nobody had written down: a development postgres on the port the tests expect,\nthe four services with their output prefixed, and the four front ends. a troubleshooting\ntable covers the traps met here.\n\nthe sign-offs tab no longer shows a placeholder for ever when the kotlin service is not\nrunning: after a few seconds it says the service is not answering.","tree":{"sha":"af67926f64238a85c069b1573d8559ae83751b21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/af67926f64238a85c069b1573d8559ae83751b21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/d313fce698982be54e22f7307a61cbe02849cbda","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"edd