om/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/b994b2be6fe86fe4368d396b292c20af76dc95ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:42:17Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:42:17Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"project settings that do something, and a margin only the product team sees\n\nprojects are the workspace''s rows now: a name, a description, a colour and a default\nassignee, edited with the version the page read and written to the feed. the default\nassignee takes every new issue that names nobody. the shell keeps no rayfold client, so it\nreads its rail from GET /projects, a query bound to a path, and the settings page tells it\nwhen to read again.\n\na product''s cost is readable by the product team only, and marked @partial: anyone else\ngets the product with that one field null and the refusal beside it in the frame, instead\nof the whole product failing. the product page shows the margin, or who it is for.","tree":{"sha":"4637dafcf41aab27396194f74f992e2b8c80a7d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/4637dafcf41aab27396194f74f992e2b8c80a7d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/b994b2be6fe86fe4368d396b292c20af76dc95ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"