ros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/20181b22b9ed2374d4d7883315f296e537d54038/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:48:14Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:48:14Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"a document belongs to a project\n\nthe documents panel listed by owner and ignored the project; every document event was pinned to p1 by an\nenvironment variable the workspace read, a seam i marked when i wrote it. now a document carries its project on\nthe row, documents(projectId) lists one project, createDocument names it, and DocumentChanged carries it — so the\nworkspace reads the project off the event and asks nothing of anyone. the variable is gone.\n\nrows from before the column existed default to the first project in the migration, which is the honest answer\nfor a deploy that already has data.\n\nverified in the browser: the second project starts empty, a file added there appears there and on its feed, and\nswitching back shows the first project''s own files and none of the second''s.","tree":{"sha":"e3e94dc9d6815e3aeda8b6e87cbccaa933a19e8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/e3e94dc9d6815e3aeda8b6e87cbccaa933a19e8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/20181b22b9ed2374d4d7883315f296e537d54038","verification":{"payload":