rl":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/614326071932b2e126f5c83cb30968c7c198234f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:36:03Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:36:03Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"the conversation on an issue\n\nclick an issue''s title and its thread opens under it: the comments, live, and a reply box. only the open thread\nsubscribes, so a list of forty issues is one live query and not forty-one.\n\nthe workspace service has tests of its own now. one pins the promise a person relies on — a thread they are\nlooking at hears a reply made from another screen — and it found a wrong assumption of mine: i had added\n`comments` to addComment''s invOp patch and written that the thread only updates because of it. it does not. the\npatch sets a Comment, and a change to any entity of a type a live query returns re-runs it; the mutation check\npassed with the op removed, so the op is gone and the comment says the real reason. the feed still needs invOp,\nbecause it returns Activity and those commands never patch one.\n\nthe other test pins the other promise: two people moving the same issue cannot both win, and the loser is told\nwhat it is now.","tree":{"sha":"cc9ead423cdd335e27e96e2556345de60a9ff712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/cc9ead423cdd335e27e96e2556345de60a9ff712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/614326071932b2e126f5c83cb30968c7c198234f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/614326071932b2e126f5c83cb30968c7c198234f","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDYxNDMyNjA3MTkzMmIyZTEyNmY1YzgzY2IzMDk2OGM3YzE5ODIzNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca","sha":"51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca"}],"sha":"614326071932b2e126f5c83cb30968c7c198234f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/614326071932b2e126f5c83cb30968c7c198234f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:27:07Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:27:07Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"one origin: a gateway in front, proxies in development\n\ninfra/gateway/nginx.conf puts the page, every remote and every service behind one host. a service is\n/api/<name>/ with the prefix stripped, a remote is /remotes/<app>/, and nothing a browser does is cross-origin: no\nservice names an allowed origin, no preflight happens, and the meta tags that told a remote where its service was\nare gone. the dev servers answer the same paths through proxy.conf.json, so a bundle is identical in both.\n\neach front end is its own container from one dockerfile, built from its own lockfile with its path as base href.\nservices publish no host port; the gateway is the only way in, as in a real deployment, and a service''s stats\nroute is reached through it with the ops token.\n\nwhat bringing it up taught, in order. postgres 18 keeps data under /var/lib/postgresql/<major>/ and refuses a\nvolume at the old .../data. nginx has to forward Host with the port — $host drops it, and a service comparing the\nbrowser''s Origin against it refused every write with 403 while curl went through. and a query that fails in a\npanel must say so: the documents panel showed \"No files yet\" for that 403, which is a lie someone acts on.\n\nverified in a browser at :8080: an issue opened through the page, the feed hearing it live, all from containers.","tree":{"sha":"a8550383741b10f6ab3fda8c0c95a067453e60cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/a8550383741b10f6ab3fda8c0c95a067453e60cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDUxZGNhNDY2Mzg2ODBlZWFkODY2NjRmMGZkZDllZmIxNDMzMzgzY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4","sha":"87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4"}],"sha":"51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/51dca46638680eead86664f0fdd9efb1433383ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:17:26Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:17:26Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"issues on the page, and a feed that hears its own service\n\nworkspace-ui exposes a second panel: open an issue, move it along. the list is live, so a move made on another\nscreen lands without a refresh, and a move sends ifVersion so two people moving the same issue cannot both win.\nthe shell lays panels out as many across as fit, so a wide screen shows the work, the files and the feed together.\n\nthe panel found a bug the tests had not. a command that writes a feed row touches no entity an open feed has\nalready read, so a live activity query was never told to re-run: the row was there on reload and invisible until\nthen. a command''s patch can name an operation — invOp — and the three feed-writing commands carry that now. the\nfleet test that covered this polled; it reads the feed live now and fails without the patch.","tree":{"sha":"6c3f0ac06ad70ea3b373cc81ef2c746bc86d32b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/6c3f0ac06ad70ea3b373cc81ef2c746bc86d32b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDg3NDg0MTkyZWRhNTYwZDFlYTYxMzE0NjJlM2JhYTJiYmJmNDU2YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e","sha":"6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e"}],"sha":"87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/87484192eda560d1ea6131462e3baa2bbbf456a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:11:50Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:11:50Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"every front end''s lockfile carries every platform''s optional entries\n\nthe matrix was fail-fast, so one leg''s missing @emnapi entries cancelled the rest and hid that all three\nlockfiles had the same gap. shell and workspace-ui are regenerated from nothing as documents-ui was, and the legs\nnow report on their own.","tree":{"sha":"1dcd367c0e59ccf503f2beb37d05c34e6e6d68b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/1dcd367c0e59ccf503f2beb37d05c34e6e6d68b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDZmOGNjZDZmYjlhN2FhOGZmNmY3NDNjMzdhZjRmNjJmYjkzMDgzNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a","sha":"3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a"}],"sha":"6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/6f8ccd6fb9a7aa8ff6f743c37af4f62fb930835e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:07:15Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:07:15Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"documents-ui: a lockfile with every platform''s optional entries\n\nnpm ci on linux refused the lockfile written on windows: it lacked @emnapi/core, runtime and wasi-threads, which\nare optional dependencies npm/cli#4828 leaves out of a lock written where they are not needed. regenerated from\nnothing, it carries them, and the ci job that installs each front end from its own lock is what caught it.","tree":{"sha":"be9890ba2a58d9a9a2b4c69ee189d2918b014dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/be9890ba2a58d9a9a2b4c69ee189d2918b014dc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDNhOWZmOWI0NmE4NGMyOWRkMmFkNmNkYjUyNTkyMDBhYzg3ZmMxM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402","sha":"54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402"}],"sha":"3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/3a9ff9b46a84c29dd2ad6cdb5259200ac87fc13a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:02:22Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:02:22Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"keel: a product, not a demo\n\na shared design system in web/design that every app builds from — cool neutrals, one accent, state colours that\nalways sit beside a word, both themes, a system type stack tuned rather than a font fetched. the shell became\nreal chrome: a rail with projects and an account, a topbar, a theme that reads the effective scheme rather than\nonly a stamped attribute, and panels that arrive with skeletons shaped like what they become.\n\ndocuments-ui is a second remote: choose or drop a file, it goes to the upload route and a command names it, and\nshare copies a capability link. the feed names the document now, because the event carries the name; before, the\nservice could only say that something changed.\n\neach remote provides its own client for its own service, from an origin the document names at runtime. the shell\nprovides none. that is what lets a bundle serve every environment and lets a panel land on any page.\n\ntwo things the browser found. native federation''s build target is a wrapper and only the esbuild target''s styles\ncount, so the design system built to nothing without a warning. and @rayfold/server 0.2.0''s preflight allow list\nomits the two upload headers, so a page on another origin could never upload — fixed upstream with a test, and\nanswered by service-kit until 0.2.1 ships.\n\nci builds each front end from its own lockfile and audits what it ships.","tree":{"sha":"97d059c4f9bb0e51b75df7ce4c3b94db3278aa6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/97d059c4f9bb0e51b75df7ce4c3b94db3278aa6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDU0Y2JlYzNlZTEwYzZjNTU0ZmZlNmVkNmY0NWJkZDUzNTIyNTU0MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7","sha":"dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7"}],"sha":"54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/54cbec3ee10c6c554ffe6ed6f45bdd5352255402"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:27:26Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:27:26Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"micro-frontends, and a reaction that survives being deployed twice\n\nweb/shell and web/workspace-ui are separate npm projects with their own lockfiles, composed at runtime with native\nfederation: the shell loads ./Feed from the remote''s remoteEntry.json and has never compiled it. the shell provides\none rayfold client for the page and the remote asks for what it needs through injectLive, so however many teams\nship into a page there is one cache and one connection.\n\ndriven in a browser: with the page open on :4200 talking only to the workspace on :4002, uploading a file to the\ndocuments service on :4001 puts a line on the feed. no refresh, no polling.\n\nthat demo found a real bug. the two services were still running while the suite ran, so two workspace instances\nboth heard DocumentChanged and both wrote a row — which is what would happen with any replica count above one. a\nreaction has to be idempotent: the row''s id is derived from what caused it and the insert says on conflict do\nnothing, so instances race and the feed gets one line. a test starts a second instance and asserts it; it fails\nwhen the id goes back to being random.\n\ntwo things the browser taught. input.required and injectLive do not mix — the query is in flight the moment it is\ninjected, which is the behaviour you want, and a required input is not readable that early (NG0950); the answer is\na default plus `enabled`, which the angular guide already documents. and `ng add` puts the federation plugin in\ndependencies, which drags webpack-dev-server into a production audit; it is a build plugin and belongs in\ndevDependencies.\n\nallowed origins are configuration now, because a front end on its own port is a cross-origin caller and a fleet\nbehind a gateway is not.","tree":{"sha":"7282a57b04e47e48e81cae2670b6be0027448a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/7282a57b04e47e48e81cae2670b6be0027448a6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKGRjNDY5Y2EzNTVmNTZlN2Y2YzcyNmQ3NGZmOGQ4OGQ1Yjg5NzgwYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2","sha":"2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2"}],"sha":"dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/dc469ca355f56e7f6c726d74ff8d88d5b89780a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:25:07Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:25:07Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"a second service, and the relay doing something only a fleet can\n\nthe workspace serves issues, comments and a project feed. the feed is the point: it carries what this service did\nand what the documents service did, and nothing is shared to make that happen.\n\ndocuments raises DocumentChanged. workspace declares that event without ever raising it and subscribes to it in\nonStart, a new hook for exactly this. the relay delivers it, the service records a line, and the live queries and\nstreams watching the feed wake up — so a query open in one service updates because of a command run in another,\nwith no shared table, no polling and no webhook.\n\ne2e/fleet.test.ts starts both services against one postgres and asserts that end to end, including a live query\nhearing it. four of its five tests fail when that one subscription is removed, which is what makes them worth\nhaving. the fifth is the one about identity, and it should not care.\n\ntwo things the schema taught: several events are listed after `emits` by name, not separated by a bar, and a\nstream returns an event type rather than an entity.\n\nalso a guard for npm/cli#4828, which has cost time in three repositories now: `pretest` says which command fixes\nit instead of a stack trace from inside vitest.","tree":{"sha":"da8c21e0b8158f45b4132387e9d26c15eb2f7422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/da8c21e0b8158f45b4132387e9d26c15eb2f7422"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKDIzMThhNDc5MzE4Mjg4ZWIwODkxMDBjNGJmZWYzMDAyZDkzYjJiYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75","sha":"d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75"}],"sha":"2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/2318a479318288eb089100c4bfef3002d93b2bb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:07:10Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T12:07:10Z","email":"eddy.boutros.36@gmail.com","name":"AdibBoutros"},"message":"a fleet of rayfold services, and the platform library they share\n\nthese are applications, not demos, and they consume the published @rayfold/* from npm exactly as anyone else does.\nthat caught something on the first typecheck: FileUploadStore is in the protocol''s working tree but not in 0.2.0,\nso service-kit carries it until 0.2.1 ships. a repository that reached into the checkout next door would not have\nnoticed until someone tried to build it.\n\nservice-kit is where the fleet decisions live, because each one is invisible until an incident: a shared\nidempotency store so a retry reaching another instance replays instead of running the command twice, a shared\nrelay so a live query hears a command run elsewhere, identity and counters so two instances can be told apart,\nreadiness that asks the database, and a SIGTERM that drains before the port closes.\n\nservices/documents is the first service. the bytes are files on a volume and the row carries their url, so nothing\nelse in the fleet learns where they are; a share is a capability token, scoped to one document and expiring on its\nown; a replace is a conditional write checked before the bytes move, and also in the update statement, since two\nreplaces arriving together must not both win.\n\na service is tested the way it is deployed: the harness sets the environment and imports the service''s own main.ts,\nso the real migration, routes and shutdown run against a real postgres. eight tests.","tree":{"sha":"8de6b213e0f4c6f6f24c58e08736afed70638363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/trees/8de6b213e0f4c6f6f24c58e08736afed70638363"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/git/commits/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50780091?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros","id":50780091,"login":"eddyboutros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzgwMDkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eddyboutros","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commit/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75","node_id":"C_kwDOUjv0ydoAKGQ4YzM1MTU1MGYwNWViY2U2M2MyZjg1ODk5NmJlZTAxYzIwMWFkNzU","parents":[],"sha":"d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits/d8c351550f05ebce63c2f858996bee01c201ad75"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/eddyboutros/rayfold-apps/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=e45e725f2bfecbbe439a81752feccf51dd3fca8f&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A56%3A21.075Z"}');
