ts (early application-id).\n- transition.RunIDFor exposes the existing deterministic run identity; both call sites use it; unit-tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016Kj1dj9VTZgtjCZuuzuG2h","tree":{"sha":"1f8921c7afacaae26112153c05f65ff31b1f41b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pr3s3nt/poc/git/trees/1f8921c7afacaae26112153c05f65ff31b1f41b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pr3s3nt/poc/git/commits/9105e608475e4cc4802574b6a48f429849806837","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f8921c7afacaae26112153c05f65ff31b1f41b1\nparent 43197010ba9f031ce5e7c39afa44a2fa50f60a43\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791435244 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791435244 +0000\n\nfix: environment-stores observer uses structural checks and proves destination ownership by deterministic transition identity\n\n- http checks asserted with jq booleans and a sorted key set, not serialized key order.\n- Cleanup deletes only the exact source namespace (this run id) and the exact generation-1 destination (name and transition run id derived from THIS application/staging/generation by the product''s own functions via the new runidentity command), each also requiring managed-by=orchestrator and environment=staging; everything else is left untouched and fails the run. Works before run.json exists (early application-id).\n- transition.RunIDFor exposes the existing deterministic run identity; both call sites use it; unit-tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016Kj1dj9VTZgtjCZuuzuG2h\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB7bjDOq\nPPQstmXkhfc4/EgwqkIO8vrZ7kAVe1dabIaslegxe36eTxX6AXGOHZWeVE38bo0d6qGlf3/NSId8\nTQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":tru