te":"2026-09-22T09:11:48Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rakesh-rajwar","providerType":"User"},"email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:46:49.789Z","repositoryId":1381098812,"sha":"0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rakesh-rajwar","providerType":"User"},"email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-22T08:30:01Z","committedDate":"2026-09-22T08:30:01Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rakesh-rajwar","providerType":"User"},"email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:46:49.789Z","repositoryId":1381098812,"sha":"2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:46:49.789Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/ad5610b4542e1f81155d4549b872b19fcd7e634e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:39:54Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:39:54Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Rebuild as the 360-platform realm, data model from the plan doc verbatim\n\nReplaces the GUM(claim)-mirrored data model with the \"Unified\nAuthorization & Identity Migration\" plan doc''s own vocabulary and worked\nexamples: realm renamed onclusive-poc -> 360-platform; customer.contract\n-> customer.entitlements (web_media/social_media, access/tier/\nsearch_limit/role - the doc''s own USER_ENTITLEMENT_UPDATED shape); new\nlegacyMapping attribute holding the doc''s Phase 0 Legacy Mapping\nDictionary (master_account_id/master_account_name/legacy_app_mappings)\nverbatim; workspaces gain isExternal to distinguish invited agencies from\ninternal sub-teams.\n\nImplements the doc''s core Phase 3 architectural concept as code, not\njust policy: a userWorkspace''s `usage` field (dynamic, e.g.\ncurrent_month_searches) is local-only and explicitly preserved by every\nrecompute path - including a full resyncAll() wipe-and-rebuild - never\nderived from or written to Keycloak, verified live through an actual\nresync.\n\n/admin becomes a two-section Customer Admin Portal (the doc''s Phase 1\npoint 4, standing in for the not-yet-existing 360 Shell): global\nentitlements (customer level) and sub-group overrides (workspace level,\n3-state inherit/override per field), both verified live end-to-end\nthrough the real webhook sync. Also confirmed live that Keycloak\nOrganizations has a native invite-by-email endpoint\n(.../members/invite-user) matching the doc''s \"invite external PR\nagencies\" ask - it works, just needs realm SMTP configured to actually\ndeliver, which this stack doesn''t set up.\n\ndemo.sh now seeds ACME Corporation using the plan doc''s own Legacy\nMapping Dictionary example verbatim, plus Marketing/Legal sub-teams and\na restricted external PR agency workspace; seed.js adds two more\ncustomers with different entitlement mixes.\n\nVerified live end-to-end from a fully clean docker compose down -v: all\n3 customers x 7 workspaces x 7 users sync correctly, entitlement edits\nvia the portal propagate through the webhook within ~2s, and usage\ncounters survive a full resync untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23533c3b7458235642e0067cfef30cabe14d8b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/23533c3b7458235642e0067cfef30cabe14d8b9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/ad5610b4542e1f81155d4549b872b19fcd7e634e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/ad5610b4542e1f81155d4549b872b19fcd7e634e","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKGFkNTYxMGI0NTQyZTFmODExNTVkNDU0OWI4NzJiMTlmY2Q3ZTYzNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2","sha":"30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2"}],"sha":"ad5610b4542e1f81155d4549b872b19fcd7e634e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/ad5610b4542e1f81155d4549b872b19fcd7e634e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:48:01Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:48:01Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Give every seeded customer multiple workspaces, fix orphan/cascade bugs\n\ndemo.sh (Acme Corp) and seed.js''s Globex previously had only one\nworkspace each, unlike Initech/Umbrella - inconsistent with the point of\nhaving multiple customers to demo featureOverrides variety. Both now\nhave two workspaces (one full-contract, one restricted), and demo.sh''s\ncontract also switched from the stale pre-catalog-update \"analyst\" key\nto real claim feature keys, matching seed.js.\n\nFound and fixed two real bugs while rebuilding this data:\n\n1. Deleting an Organization in Keycloak doesn''t fire separate\n   ORGANIZATION_GROUP/ORGANIZATION_GROUP_MEMBERSHIP delete events for\n   its child org-groups - they just vanish upstream, leaving orphaned\n   workspaces/userWorkspaces rows locally. syncCustomer/syncWorkspace\n   now cascade those deletes themselves. Reproduced live: recreating a\n   deleted customer produced duplicate stale rows before this fix.\n\n2. Added resyncAll() (POST /admin/resync, plus a \"Full resync\" button\n   on the dashboard) as the repair path for whatever''s already\n   orphaned, or for any missed webhook delivery generally - walks every\n   Organization -> org-group -> member currently in Keycloak and\n   rebuilds customers/workspaces/users/userWorkspaces from scratch\n   (wipe-and-rebuild via new db.replaceAll(), not additive upserts).\n   Had to fetch each org/group''s *detail* representation, not just its\n   list-endpoint summary - verified live that Keycloak''s list endpoints\n   omit the attributes field entirely, only the single-entity GET has\n   it.\n\nVerified live end-to-end: all 4 customers x 9 workspaces x 9 users now\nsync with correct per-workspace featureOverrides and enabledFeatures,\nno duplicates, confirmed via both curl and the dashboard''s resync\nbutton.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92d3c54fbebd7c1b366acb66ec4a18e69ce2271d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/92d3c54fbebd7c1b366acb66ec4a18e69ce2271d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDMwZjQ3NDE5ZjJjOWQzYmJjMmM2Mzc2ODMwZGE2N2IyYWMyNGYwYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42","sha":"7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42"}],"sha":"30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/30f47419f2c9d3bbc2c6376830da67b2ac24f0a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:55:55Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:55:55Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Generalize register-webhook.sh to take URL/secret/eventTypes args\n\nWebhook registration is REST-only (confirmed against the extension''s own\ndocs - no Admin Console page exists for the subscription itself, only\nfor the event-listener toggle), and it''s additive rather than a single\nslot - each POST creates an independent subscription, verified live by\nregistering a second URL and confirming both coexisted with distinct\nids before cleanup.\n\nregister-webhook.sh took a fixed consumer-app URL/secret from env vars\nonly, meaning adding a second consumer meant hand-writing the curl call.\nNow takes them as positional args (URL, SECRET, EVENT_TYPES - comma-\nseparated, default \"*\"), falling back to the original env vars/defaults\nwhen called with no args so existing callers are unaffected. Verified\nlive: no-args call still targets consumer-app correctly; an args-based\ncall with a filtered eventTypes list correctly registered as a second,\nindependent subscription alongside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"562f91b39ebbf4ca90c924056737d9e80488fec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/562f91b39ebbf4ca90c924056737d9e80488fec6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDcwMzY1MDYwODliNmYzY2Y5NjBiMWU4YmI1MjVjYTljNjBhYjlkNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413","sha":"73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413"}],"sha":"7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/7036506089b6f3cf960b1e8bb525ca9c60ab9d42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:48:26Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:48:26Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Add multi-customer seed script and use claim''s real feature catalog\n\nscripts/seed.js adds three more customers on top of demo.sh''s single\nAcme Corp walkthrough, deliberately varied: Globex (simple, one\nworkspace), Initech (two workspaces - a full-access default and an\ninternal team restricted via featureOverrides), and Umbrella PR Agency\n(three workspaces, one per sub-client, each with a different override) -\nthe last one is the exact multi-tenant-under-one-customer case\nworkspaces.featureOverrides''s own schema comment describes (\"for PR\nagencies, etc.\").\n\nfeatureCatalog.js''s keys/names/grouping are now copied directly from\nclaim''s prisma/seed.js FEATURE_CATALOG (mentions/mentions.cm/mentions.360,\ncontacts.prmanager, review.rep, geo/analytics-basic/analytics-premium)\ninstead of the placeholder mentions/analyst catalog - both seed.js and\nthe /admin checkbox editor now reflect real product features.\n\nVerified live: all 3 customers x 6 workspaces x 6 users synced correctly\nvia webhook, with per-workspace featureOverrides correctly reflected in\neach user''s enabledFeatures (e.g. Initech''s finance workspace correctly\ndrops review.rep/analytics-premium for its one user while the default\nworkspace keeps the full 8-feature contract).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2582c7395a6d8a781ad424f099fe21cc8a8c7bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/b2582c7395a6d8a781ad424f099fe21cc8a8c7bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDczZTg0MTZjYjgwZDJmNDYxYWZhMzBiNzQ2NGY4MDQ4MzQxNTQ0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be","sha":"76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be"}],"sha":"73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/73e8416cb80d2f461afa30b7464f804834154413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:39:08Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T07:39:08Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Add /admin contract-features checkbox editor\n\nKeycloak''s own Attributes tab (Organizations and Groups alike) is a fixed\ngeneric key/value text editor - there''s no config or theming hook to make\na specific attribute render as anything richer, so hand-typing JSON was\nthe only option. This adds a small purpose-built form instead: pick a\ncustomer, check/uncheck features, save - it translates the selection into\ncontract.featureSets JSON and PATCHes the Organization via the Admin REST\nAPI, same as the rest of this PoC.\n\nMirrors claim''s own contract-features editor UX (views/partials/\ncontract-features-edit.eta): parent/child checkboxes, single-child\nparents toggle in lockstep with their one child, multi-child parents\nrequire at least one enabled child. Deliberately skips claim''s\nimpact-preview modal (which customers/users would be affected) since\nthat needs the reachability engine this PoC doesn''t reproduce - saves\napply directly and flow back through the normal webhook sync like every\nother change here (including the enabledFeatures recomputation fix from\nearlier).\n\nVerified live: toggling a feature off correctly updates the customer''s\ncontract and recomputes enabledFeatures for every affected membership;\nsingle-child lockstep (unchecking the only child auto-unchecks its\nparent) confirmed working in-browser.\n\nNew: consumer-app/src/adminForm.js, consumer-app/src/featureCatalog.js\nChanged: keycloakAdmin.js (updateOrganization), server.js (GET /admin,\nPOST /admin/customers/:orgId/contract-features), README\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e5b5314d7971d285a90e1a0a808e3f9dc829e5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/8e5b5314d7971d285a90e1a0a808e3f9dc829e5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDc2NjU1ODU3YTNmMjM2ZjRlNGNiODE2MmYxYjhmZTc2NDEyMzU4YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e","sha":"15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e"}],"sha":"76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/76655857a3f236f4e4cb8162f1b8fe76412358be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:56:23Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:56:23Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Add Porter deployment doc for a demo instance\n\nDocuments deploying this PoC as two Porter apps (keycloak, consumer-app)\nwith no database service - Keycloak''s start-dev falls back to its\nembedded dev store when KC_DB isn''t set, and consumer-app''s local \"DB\"\nis already just a JSON file, so nothing needs provisioning for a demo.\n\nIncludes the exact porter create/env var/webhook-registration commands,\nand calls out what''s lost versus local docker-compose: no persistence\nacross restarts, and the same PoC-grade plaintext credentials now\nreachable publicly rather than just on localhost.\n\nNo Porter commands were run against any project - this is documentation\nonly, for the user to execute against their own new Porter project.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e655344254d36e52a74f95ee0295ffb3cf2118a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/5e655344254d36e52a74f95ee0295ffb3cf2118a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDE1Y2Q4YmFmMjY3ZjAwYzgzOWU4ZWU5ZTNjNDllZTc1OThlNjQ0OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8","sha":"847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8"}],"sha":"15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/15cd8baf267f00c839e8ee9e3c49ee7598e6448e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:35:03Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:35:03Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Recompute enabledFeatures when a contract or featureOverrides changes\n\nPreviously enabledFeatures was only derived once, at the moment a\nuserWorkspace membership was created - a later change to the customer''s\ncontract or the workspace''s featureOverrides left existing memberships\nstale until their own membership event fired again (a real gap called\nout in the README and demonstrated live in conversation).\n\nAdds recomputeEnabledFeaturesForCustomer()/ForWorkspace(), called from\nthe ORGANIZATION and ORGANIZATION_GROUP update handlers respectively,\nwhich re-derive enabledFeatures for every already-synced userWorkspace\nscoped to that customer/workspace. Verified live both directions:\nchanging a contract''s featureSets and clearing a workspace''s\nfeatureOverrides both now update every affected membership in the same\nwebhook round-trip.\n\nThis is bounded local recomputation only, not GUM''s full\nreachability-diffing engine (event-fanout.ts) - it fixes staleness in\nconsumer-app''s own table, it doesn''t re-emit change events to other\ndownstream apps. README updated to describe the fix and that remaining\nscope gap precisely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2323446030ad69d4e46aa61b9829ebd792af4398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/2323446030ad69d4e46aa61b9829ebd792af4398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDg0NzQ2MGJmMjg2MmZiNmMwYzIxNWZiOTY0ZThiNThlNDIyZDkzYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de","sha":"6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de"}],"sha":"847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/847460bf2862fb6c0c215fb964e8b58e422d93a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:20:24Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:20:24Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Source customers.isActive from Keycloak''s native enabled field\n\nDrop the redundant isActive custom attribute - it was just parroting a\nstatic value with no derivation logic behind it. Prefer Keycloak''s native\nOrganization.enabled field instead, per the general principle of using\nnative platform features over custom attributes where one actually fits.\n\nREADME documents the real semantic gap this leaves: GUM''s isActive is a\ncomputed state (checkAndUpdateAccountActivation - derived from contract\nvalidity, feature reachability, workspace/user existence, auto-deactivate\nonly / manual re-activate), whereas Keycloak''s enabled is a flat admin\ntoggle with no derivation behind it. Verified live both directions\n(enabled: true/false correctly flows through to customers.isActive).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c9c84523eca5b673b58313898ef8b34cc0948b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/0c9c84523eca5b673b58313898ef8b34cc0948b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDZkODFmNTdlMGFkYTYxZDYzZTVjZDdlMGMyOGZkZDZiMTg2ZmExZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf","sha":"0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf"}],"sha":"6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/6d81f57e0ada61d63e5cd7e0c28fdd6b186fa1de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:11:48Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:11:48Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Remodel PoC hierarchy to mirror GUM''s (claim) real entities\n\nReplace the generic Organization/subscriptions-group model with a 1:1\nmirror of shared-services/claim''s actual schema: customers (Keycloak\nOrganization + attributes), workspaces (Keycloak 26.6+ organization-scoped\nGroups, replacing the earlier attribute-linked top-level group hack), and\nuserWorkspaces membership, with a customer''s 1:1 contract flattened onto\nthe Organization as a JSON attribute since Keycloak has no native entity\nfor it. enabledFeatures per membership is now derived from the contract +\nworkspace featureOverrides, mirroring GUM''s applicationGrants concept\ninstead of the ad hoc realm roles the previous version used.\n\nVerified live end-to-end against a fresh stack, including two real\nKeycloak API quirks found only by triggering events and reading raw\npayloads: collection-POST admin events omit the created resource''s id\nfrom resourcePath (worked around via event.details/representation), and\norg-group membership requires prerequisite plain org membership. README\ndocuments the full GUM<->Keycloak mapping and the known gap versus GUM''s\nreachability-diffing webhook fan-out (event-fanout.ts), which this PoC\ndoes not reproduce.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cf04d091b2c06cba571b23bf8f491e1a1784890","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/5cf04d091b2c06cba571b23bf8f491e1a1784890"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf","node_id":"C_kwDOUlHlPNoAKDA4NjBjYmRjZTBjNGY3MTViNWE4Nzg0Yjg5M2E3MDRlYmRkMWVhYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commit/2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba","sha":"2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba"}],"sha":"0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/0860cbdce0c4f715b5a8784b893a704ebdd1eabf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19924569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rakesh-rajwar","id":19924569,"login":"rakesh-rajwar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0NTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rakesh-rajwar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/commits/2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:30:01Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:30:01Z","email":"rakesh.chand@onclusive.com","name":"Rakesh Chand"},"message":"Add Phase 1 PoC: Keycloak as out-of-band source of truth\n\nStands up Keycloak 26.6.3 + the keycloak-events webhook extension,\na realm modeling Organizations/subscriptions/roles, and a downstream\nconsumer-app that syncs its own local tables purely from Keycloak\nAdmin Event Webhooks. Validated end-to-end (create/update/delete\nflowing through for orgs, subscription groups, users, and org\nmemberships with role mappings) against a live docker compose stack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db4580f023644df39cb7ed769e612695a84828df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/trees/db4580f023644df39cb7ed769e612695a84828df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rakesh-rajwar/keycloak-poc/git/commits/2199480a75791f54ceac38a5dc658a250b1ad4ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature"