/users/deathbyorderfill/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathbyorderfill/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathbyorderfill","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deathbyorderfill/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-SD-Single-Spark/commits/4b33740cd3862470381147d409ee62ff79488c76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:27:08Z","email":"jonathanthomascho22@gmail.com","name":"deathbyorderfill"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:28:10Z","email":"jonathanthomascho22@gmail.com","name":"deathbyorderfill"},"message":"Update benchmarks to the published run; make chart and hero reproducible\n\nSpeed figures now come from speed_published.json rather than the earlier\nml_dv2 run: single-stream prose 32.2, code 36.7, math 38.8 tok/s and a\n3-stream aggregate of 57.7 tok/s (was 28.8 / 38.2 / 38.8 and 51.8). Code is\nslightly down, prose and aggregate up; all within the documented +/-5 %.\n\nAggregate is 1200 completion tokens / longest stream wall time. Summing the\nper-stream decode rates gives 60.9 and overstates delivered throughput, so\nthe README now states the definition explicitly.\n\ndocs/make_benchmarks.py regenerates the chart straight from the probe JSON so\nthe two cannot drift apart, and speed_nospec.json (the no-speculation\nbaseline the chart compares against) is checked in beside it.\ndocs/make_hero.py composites the figures over generated art for docs/hero.png.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe319c8ee89f8365d7d1bdd1e71a9927545862e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deathbyorderfill/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-SD-Single-Spark/git/trees/fe319c8ee89f8365d7d1bdd1e71a9927545862e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deathbyorderfill/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-SD-Single-Spark/git/commits/4b33740cd3862470381147d409ee62ff79488c76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":nul